From cbc1655bbe82bbf7d32554e43d9c54523efd9a05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z-Vibes <180806113+z-Vibes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:32:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bake: split pages draw the nearest colour their row holds,
 never confetti

A texel's 4-bit index only means something against the CLUT row it is drawn
with. On a page whose colours do not fit one 16-entry row, three things broke
that and drew panels as "confetti":

- Out of texture ids: a group past id 31 kept its material's id and
  OVERWROTE that row, so the material's first group drew with another
  group's 16 colours. It now takes an id no material names, and only when
  none is left shares the row that fits it best (_share_row): that row's
  free slots take the group's costliest missing colours, and the rest map
  to the nearest colour the row holds.
- Wrong row for a split poly: the centroid rule let any first-row rect of
  the same material win, so a poly the splitter moved to a second row was
  drawn with the first. carbank_page.row_for_poly is now the one rule (a
  piece whose rect IS the poly's UV bbox wins) and carbank_bake._id_at asks
  it, so the planner and the bake cannot disagree.
- Overlapping bboxes: a later group re-indexed texels an earlier group's
  polys draw. reconcile_rows checks every drawn texel against the row its
  poly uses and moves a wrong one to its exact colour, a free slot, or the
  nearest colour (perceptual distance; a texel two rows share gets the slot
  nearest in both). Visible texels never move onto a slot pack_indexed
  clears for transparency, and a page with nothing wrong keeps its bytes.

Also:
- Identical UV bboxes (clean/damaged/low share an unwrap) no longer open a
  new quantize group each, which burned ids.
- A material id of 32 or more gets a row the engine holds.
- PLANNER_VERSION joins each page's source record, so old pages re-bake once.
- --check hashed pages without their UV islands and called every textured
  page STALE; it now hashes what the bake hashed.
- D1 bake: more than 32 flat colours no longer stops the bake; the most-used
  32 keep rows and the rest draw with the nearest kept colour. A page whose
  cars use more than 32 texture ids is named in a warning.

Measured on the original planner with the new test scenes: 80, 171 and 400
texels drawn with the wrong palette; after: 0, 0 and 0. tools/car: 234 tests
pass (18 skipped, as before); tools/common: 31 pass.

